## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of multi-account Terraform setups with minimal code duplication, demonstrating proficiency with provider aliases, wrapper modules, and CI gates to enforce environment boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- Provider aliases for multi-account AWS access
- Backend/workspace separation for state isolation
- Wrapper modules for environment context management
- CI gates to enforce production change protections

## Code Example
```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.0"
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "terraform-state-bucket"
    key    = "${terraform.workspace}/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "prod"
  region = "us-east-1"
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "sandbox"
  region = "us-east-1"
}

module "environment" {
  source = "./modules/environment-wrapper"
  providers = {
    aws = terraform.workspace == "prod" ? aws.prod : aws.sandbox
  }
  environment = terraform.workspace
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-cloud, multi-env orchestration, and robust gating. It probes backend scoping, provider aliasing, and policy-as-code integration in a realistic production-like flow.

## Key Concepts
- Per-env Terraform backends and state isolation
- Provider aliasing for multi-cloud deployments
- Policy-as-code gates (Sentinel/OPA) for prod safety
- Wrapper modules for consistent tagging across clouds

## Code Example
```javascript
// backend.tf (Terraform S3 backend per environment)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "org-terraform"
    key    = "state/${var.environment}/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

```javascript
// Providers with aliases (multi-cloud)
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
  alias  = "aws"
}
provider "google" {
  project = var.gcp_project
  region  = var.gcp_region
  alias   = "gcp"
}
```

```javascript
// Wrapper module usage for tags
module "shared_tags" {
  source      = "./modules/tags"
  environment = var.environment
  cost_center = var.cost_center
}
```

```javascript
// Simple OPA/rego style policy (example)
package terraform.policy
default allow = false
allow {
  input.environment != "prod"
}
```

```javascript
// CI gate steps (high level)
terraform init
terraform plan -out=tfplan
terraform show -json tfplan > plan.json
# Evaluate plan.json against policy (opa or sentinel)
```
